[ti:The Cutty Sark]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.32]Lesson 25 | 第25课
[00:02.35]The Cutty Sark | “卡蒂萨克”号帆船
[00:09.48]What piece of bad luck prevented the Cutty Sark from winning the race? | 是什么厄运使“卡蒂萨克”号帆船输掉了那场比赛？
[00:16.14]One of the most famous sailing ships of the nineteenth century, the Cutty Sark, can still be seen at Greenwich. | 19世纪最有名的帆船之一“卡蒂萨克”号，如今仍然陈列在格林威治。
[00:24.39]She stands on dry land and is visited by thousands of people each year. | 它停在陆地上，每年接待成千上万的参观者。
[00:30.28]She serves as an impressive reminder of the great ships of the past. | 它给人们留下深刻的印象，使人回想起历史上的巨型帆船。
[00:36.09]Before they were replaced by steamships, | 在蒸汽船取代帆船之前，
[00:39.07]sailing vessels like the Cutty Sark were used to carry tea from China and wool from Australia. | 像“卡蒂萨克”号这样的帆船被用来从中国运茶叶，从澳大利亚运羊毛。
[00:47.25]The Cutty Sark was one of the fastest sailing ships that has ever been built. | “卡蒂萨克”号是建造过的最快的帆船之一。
[00:53.22]The only other ship to match her was the Thermopylae. | 唯一能与之匹敌的船是“塞姆皮拉”号。
[00:58.15]Both these ships set out from Shanghai on June 18th, 1872 on an exciting race to England. | 两船于1872年6月18日同时从上海启程，驶往英国，展开了一场激动人心的比赛。
[01:07.82]This race, which went on for exactly four months, was the last of its kind. | 这场比赛整整持续了4个月，是此类比赛的最后一次。
[01:14.61]It marked the end of the great tradition of ships with sails and the beginning of a new era. | 它标志着帆船伟大传统的结束和新纪元的开始。
[01:22.51]The first of the two ships to reach Java after the race had begun was the Thermopylae, | 比赛开始后率先到达爪哇的是“塞姆皮拉”号，
[01:29.60]but on the Indian Ocean, the Cutty Sark took the lead. | 但在印度洋上，“卡蒂萨克”号驶到了前面。
[01:33.88]It seemed certain that she would be the first ship home, | 看来它率先返抵英国是确信无疑的了，
[01:37.67]but during the race she had a lot of bad luck. | 但它在比赛中连遭厄运。
[01:41.86]In August, she was struck by a very heavy storm during which her rudder was torn away. | 8月份，它遭到一场特大风暴的袭击，舵被冲走了。
[01:49.43]The Cutty Sark rolled from side to side and it became impossible to steer her. | “卡蒂萨克”号左右摇摆，无法驾驭。
[01:55.93]A temporary rudder was made on board from spare planks and it was fitted with great difficulty. | 船员们用备用的厚木板赶制了一只应急舵，费了好大的劲才把它安装好。
[02:03.64]This greatly reduced the speed of the ship, for there was a danger that if she travelled too quickly, | 这大大降低了船速，因为船一旦行驶太快，
[02:10.86]this rudder would be torn away as well. | 这只舵就有可能被冲走。
[02:14.60]Because of this, the Cutty Sark lost her lead. | 因为这个缘故，“卡蒂萨克”号落到了后面。
[02:18.74]After crossing the Equator, the captain called in at a port to have a new rudder fitted, | 穿过赤道后，船长进港加装了一只新舵，
[02:25.65]but by now the Thermopylae was over five hundred miles ahead. | 但此时“塞姆皮拉”号已经领先500多英里了。
[02:30.98]Though the new rudder was fitted at tremendous speed, it was impossible for the Cutty Sark to win. | 尽管新舵装得极快，但“卡蒂萨克”号已经不可能获胜了。
[02:39.18]She arrived in England a week after the Thermopylae. | 它抵达英国时比“塞姆皮拉”号晚了一个星期。
[02:43.39]Even this was remarkable, considering that she had had so many delays. | 考虑到它曾在途中多次耽搁，这已经很不容易了。
[02:49.29]There is no doubt that if she had not lost her rudder she would have won the race easily. | 毫无疑问，如果它没有失去舵，它本可以轻易夺冠。
